Sections "MS" contain missmatched items: {'MS_COMMENTS': ["Targeted LC-MS/MS analysis was performed using a Waters Xevo TQ-XS electrospray ionization tandem quadrupole mass spectrometer in positive-ion multiple reaction monitoring (MRM) mode. The capillary voltage, sampling cone voltage, and desolvation temperature were 2.5 kV, 30 V, and 400°C, respectively. Data were acquired and processed using MassLynx version 4.2, SCN 1012 (Waters). The values submitted to Metabolomics Workbench are integrated chromatographic peak areas, without internal-standard normalization or conversion to within-class percentages. Internal-standard peak areas are included as separate entries. Phospholipid annotation was based on peaks observed in purified lipid-class standard mixtures obtained from Avanti, together with MRM transitions and retention times. Lipid species were reported at the sum-composition level; structural isomers, including those differing in double-bond positions, were not distinguished. For downstream analyses reported in the publication, phospholipid peak areas were normalized to the corresponding internal-standard peak areas. Within-class compositions were calculated by expressing each species' internal-standard-normalized value as a percentage of the sum of these values within the corresponding lipid class. Where applicable, internal-standard-normalized values were further normalized to cell number. PS species with a mass shift of +7 Da following stable-isotope serine labeling were analyzed to assess de novo synthesis and are listed separately from unlabeled PS species. Free cholesterol was analyzed after acetyl derivatization using d7-cholesterol as an internal standard; the submitted peak areas correspond to the acetylated analyte and internal standard.", "Targeted LC-MS/MS analysis was performed using a Waters Xevo TQ-XS electrospray ionization tandem quadrupole mass spectrometer in positive-ion multiple reaction monitoring (MRM) mode. The capillary voltage, sampling cone voltage, and desolvation temperature were 2.5 kV, 30 V, and 400°C, respectively. Data were acquired and processed using MassLynx version 4.2, SCN 1012 (Waters). The values submitted to Metabolomics Workbench are integrated chromatographic peak areas, without internal-standard normalization or conversion to within-class percentages. Internal-standard peak areas are included as separate entries. Phospholipid annotation was based on peaks observed in purified lipid-class standard mixtures obtained from Avanti, together with MRM transitions and retention times. Lipid species were reported at the sum-composition level; structural isomers, including those differing in double-bond positions, were not distinguished. For downstream analyses reported in the publication, phospholipid peak areas were normalized to the corresponding internal-standard peak areas. Within-class compositions were calculated by expressing each species'' internal-standard-normalized value as a percentage of the sum of these values within the corresponding lipid class. Where applicable, internal-standard-normalized values were further normalized to cell number. PS species with a mass shift of +7 Da following stable-isotope serine labeling were analyzed to assess de novo synthesis and are listed separately from unlabeled PS species. Free cholesterol was analyzed after acetyl derivatization using d7-cholesterol as an internal standard; the submitted peak areas correspond to the acetylated analyte and internal standard."]}